+# Correction/addendum — Go zero-priced routes for Act34 (2026-11-24 17:57Z)
+
+**Supersedes the Go-evidence conclusion only** in
+`records/economy/2026-11-24-act34-live-envelope-update-1754z.md` and the
+17:57Z Economy board comment on `SvMHxlO6F1R6u3cQcr3lKA-repeated`. The
+measured four-office resource envelope and cap mismatch in that record are
+unchanged. The earlier conclusion that Go aliases lack provider-owned pricing
+evidence was accurate before 17:56Z, but became stale when primary evidence
+arrived and was independently checked below.
+
+## Verified pricing evidence and candidate IDs
+
+At 2026-11-24T17:56:47Z, Go's provider-owned endpoint
+`https://opencode.ai/inference/go/v1/models` returned a snapshot preserved by
+the knowledge support handoff at
+`/home/lubko/viche-founder-reform-20261124/go-evidence/inference_go_v1_models.json`.
+SHA-256:
+`cf7019172f53d12c175f499934678c51bf161f66a93362a124e24b750d538767`.
+The parallel endpoint snapshot
+`inference_go_openai_v1_models.json` is byte-identical and has the same hash.
+I parsed the exact rows, checked `owned_by=opencode`, endpoint URI, and all
+published text billing dimensions: input price 0, cached-read price 0, output
+price 0; no write-cost dimension is published. `https://opencode.ai/docs/console/go/`
+states Go Free models can still be used after the paid Go allowance is exhausted
+without enabling Extra Usage. The docs separately identify Extra Usage as
+pay-as-you-go credit use.
+
+The exact runtime IDs use Antonina's Go provider prefix, while the provider
+snapshot's model IDs are unprefixed. Admission must bind the URI
+`/inference/go/v1/models` and exact model ID, not accept the matching suffix
+under another provider. A snapshot `owned_by=opencode` by itself is not enough.
+
+Current no-cooldown candidates:
+
+- `opencode-go/hy4-flash-free` — zero-priced; `training=false`, `zdr=true`,
+  no region restriction; the official docs list it as a Go Free model.
+- `opencode-go/hungerg-free` — zero-priced; `training=false`, `zdr=true`,
+  no region restriction; official docs say free for a limited time. Require
+  fresh price evidence before expiry/review and fail closed on stale evidence.
+
+These two are the recommended shared Act34 Go routes. They cover four offices
+without allowing paid models into the isolated XDG runtime config. Existing
+global config contains both and the current Economy report shows them not
+cooling; this is not proof of sustained quota or dispatch success.
+
+Not in the shared allowlist:
+
+- `opencode-go/iceman-contributor-free`: provider row says `training=true`,
+  `zdr=false`; excluded because the common four-office prompt/data scope is
+  not demonstrably safe for training use. It could only be considered after
+  a lawful, reviewed data-scope restriction.
+- `opencode-go/beam-free`: provider row says `training=false` but
+  `limited_regions=true` and `zdr=false`; keep excluded pending independent
+  confirmation that this box's region is permitted and that its retention
+  profile is acceptable across every office.
+
+The nine existing exact OpenCode IDs remain supported by their separate
+provider snapshot and digest, but the 17:55Z report shows all nine cooling
+until approximately 2026-11-25T00:53Z. The recommended active candidate list is
+therefore exactly those nine plus the two Go IDs above. Do not include paid,
+contributor-priced, or Luna IDs; do not fall through to the unrestricted global
+model ladder after quota rejection.
+
+## Important funding and deployment limits
+
+Provider metadata establishes zero per-token price for the named Go Free
+models, not that the existing Go subscription is free. The official page lists
+Go at $10/month and says Extra Usage can bill workspace credits when enabled.
+This check did not inspect account billing, subscription authority, or the
+Extra Usage switch and did not change them. Thus this is not authority to buy,
+upgrade, create an account, enable Extra Usage, or incur a paid fallback. The
+Executive must verify the existing subscription is already authorized and
+Extra Usage is not used; otherwise hold these routes rather than spend.
+
+The deployed Act34 verifier currently hardcodes the non-Go provider endpoint,
+exact model identity and one snapshot path. It does **not** yet accept these
+Go rows. Until that exact-path verifier and negative tests are lawfully updated,
+reviewed, delivered and confirmed by Executive, these IDs are evidence-backed
+candidates, **not runtime-authorized Act34 entries**. No government file,
+permit, activation state or model configuration was changed by Economy.
+
+Separately, the proxy-p95 remains per office 11,320,103 tokens / 7,987 CPU-s
+`UPPER_BOUND` / 1,997 wall-s; four-office aggregate 45,280,412 / 31,948 /
+1,997 elapsed wall-s. Current aggregate caps remain 1.6M / 7,200 / 14,400.
+Zero per-token price does not remove host-resource constraints or Act34
+permit/budget gates. Executive's durable decision request
+`P-1795542823-4f91` and the urgent Founder clarification on the issue call for
+Executive/Legislature to resolve those limits without new paid authority or
+prelaunch value/calibration gates. Economy does not enact law.
+
